== line 34: The Tax Foundation's tables: used with attribution (default) or replaced by the statutes
which figures rest on them: sales_tax.json (state and average local rate, 51 rows, 'Tax Foundation, State and Local Sales Tax Rates, Midyear 2026') and income_tax.json (brackets, 51 rows, 'Tax Foundation, State Individual Income Tax Rates and Brackets, 2026'): every sales and income tax figure. Replaced by the statutes, a state's own rate and brackets are the statute's figures and would not move where the Foundation copied them right; the average local rate has no statute (the Foundation's population-weighted mean): left out, the page as it opens reads sales and use tax 19.92 million -> 15.18 million (-23.8%, the state's 6.25 percent alone). New York gas as an income-tax case: income tax over the life 45.65 million, which rests on the brackets

